## 1. Context

Repositories already contain human-authored markdown (specs, design docs, incident write-ups) that encodes rules a change should respect, but review agents never see it. This feature lets a user browse every `.md` document under a repo's configured root context folders (default `specs`/`docs`/`insights`), attach documents (by path, never by copied text) to an agent's Context tab or a skill's "Project context to use" section, and have those documents read fresh from the repo clone and injected &#x2014; untrusted-wrapped &#x2014; into the reviewer's existing `## Project context` prompt slot at run time. Attachment is manual only in this iteration (no automatic per-PR selection). This is a read-only feature end to end: no in-browser editing of the documents themselves.

This plan also retires a pre-existing, unimplemented "context browser" scaffold (dead hooks/contracts/route reservation from an earlier, unrelated "embedding-indexed spec chunks" concept) and **repurposes** its route path, sidebar nav key, and i18n namespace for the real feature &#x2014; see Step 1.

## 2. Architecture Fit

**New server module &#x2014; `server/src/modules/context-docs/`** (routes/service/repository/helpers), registered statically in `modules/index.ts`, following the exact pattern of `blast/` and `repo-intel/`:
- `repository.ts` &#x2014; Drizzle queries against a new `context_documents` attachment table (agent/skill link rows) and the new `repos.context_folders` column; every query workspace-scoped through a join to `repos`/`agents`/`skills`.
- `service.ts` &#x2014; discovery (walk clone dir under configured root folders), token counting (`container.tokenizer`), used-by-count aggregation, attach/detach/reorder orchestration. No adapter is imported directly &#x2014; `container.git.readFile` / `container.git.clonePathFor` / `container.tokenizer.count` only. Discovery + per-document token counts are **cached** (see �4 Caching) so the full clone walk + tokenization does not run on every request.
- `routes.ts` &#x2014; `GET /repos/:id/context-docs` (list + discovery), `GET /repos/:id/context-docs/:encodedPath` (single doc preview text), `PUT /repos/:id/context-folders` (AC-21), plus two sub-routes attached to the **existing** `agents` and `skills` route files (not a new plugin) for attach/detach/reorder, mirroring `POST /agents/:id/skills`.

**Run-time wiring** &#x2014; `run-executor.ts` gains one new step (parallel to the existing skills-injection block at `runOneAgent`): resolve attached document paths (agent-direct &#x222a; via attached skills, deduped), read each through `container.git.readFile` with path confinement, count tokens, build the `specs: string[]` array, and pass it into `reviewPullRequest({ ..., specs })`. `reviewer-core/src/prompt.ts` needs **zero changes** &#x2014; the `specs?: string[]` slot and its `wrapUntrusted('spec-N', &#x2026;)` wrapping already exist and are exercised for the first time by this feature.

**`@devdigest/shared` contract additions** (mirrored in both `server/src/vendor/shared/` and `client/src/vendor/shared/` in the same step): `ContextDocument`, `ContextDocumentAttachment`-adjacent request/response shapes, `RunTraceContextDoc` + `context_documents` field on `RunTrace`.

**Dead-scaffolding retirement + repurposing (Step 1, before any new code)** &#x2014; the client currently carries unimplemented plumbing from an earlier, different "Project Context" concept (embedding-indexed spec chunks with editable text and an index-status model): `useContextFiles`/`useReindexContext` hooks (`client/src/lib/hooks/core.ts`), the Zod `SpecFile`/`IndexStatus` contracts in `vendor/shared/contracts/platform.ts` (both copies), their re-export in `client/src/lib/types.ts`, and a stale doc-comment in `client/src/lib/hooks/repo-intel.ts`. These are deleted. The `/repos/[repoId]/context` route path, the `"context"` sidebar nav key (`activeKeyFor()` in `app-shell/helpers.ts`), and the `context.json` i18n namespace file are **kept and repurposed** for the real Project Context page built in this feature &#x2014; the file/route/nav-key identity survives, its (dead) contents do not.

**Client** &#x2014; the page at `client/src/app/repos/[repoId]/context/page.tsx` (new content, existing route path), a new `ContextTab` component in the Agent Editor (sibling to the existing `SkillsTab`), a new "Project context to use" section in `SkillDetail`'s `ConfigTab`, and a new trace section in `TraceBody` for injected/skipped context documents.

## 3. Skills & Patterns Applied

**`backend-onion-architecture`:**
- New module = `routes.ts` / `service.ts` / `repository.ts` / `helpers.ts` under `src/modules/context-docs/`, registered in `modules/index.ts` (R7).
- `service.ts` never imports concrete adapters &#x2014; `container.git`, `container.tokenizer` only (R2).
- Every repository query scoped by `workspace_id` via a join (attachments have no direct `workspace_id` column &#x2014; they join through `agents`/`skills`, both of which do; the *document listing* query is scoped by `repos.workspace_id`) (R1).
- Expected failures (`repo not found`, `path outside clone`) &#x2192; `NotFoundError` / `ValidationError`, never raw `Error` (R3).
- No cross-module internal imports: the new module never imports `agents/service.ts` or `skills/service.ts` internals; the agent/skill attach routes live in *their own* route files and call into `context-docs`' service via `container`-free direct construction (same pattern as `AgentsService` constructing `AgentsRepository` &#x2014; a small `ContextDocsRepository` is instantiated directly inside `agents/service.ts` and `skills/service.ts` is **not** done; instead see Step 4 for the exact ownership split that avoids this).

**`typescript-expert`:**
- `RunTraceContextDoc` as a discriminated-ish object (`status: 'injected' | 'skipped'`, `skip_reason` nullable) &#x2014; exported type + Zod schema together (`type-export-schemas-and-types`).
- `z.infer` for all new DTOs, no manual interface duplication.
- Additive-only changes to `RunTrace`/`PromptAssembly`-adjacent shared types &#x2014; old persisted JSONB traces lack `context_documents`, so the field is `.nullish()` or defaulted via `.default([])`, matching the existing `specs_read: z.array(z.string())` non-nullable-with-safe-default pattern used elsewhere in `trace.ts`.
- Dead-code removal (Step 1) is a mechanical, verifiable operation: grep for zero remaining references to each deleted symbol before considering the deletion done ("Missing type declarations"/module-resolution failures are the signal a reference was missed).

**`zod`:**
- Request schemas (`AttachContextDocsBody`, `UpdateContextFoldersBody`) validated at the route boundary, one schema drives both validation and the TS type (`schema-use-primitives-correctly`, `parse-validate-early`).
- `z.array(z.string()).min(0)` for `document_paths` &#x2014; empty array is a valid "detach all" state, not an error.

**`drizzle-orm-patterns` / `postgresql-table-design`:**
- New link tables `agent_context_docs` / `skill_context_docs` follow the exact shape of `agent_skills` (composite PK `(ownerId, path)`, `order integer not null default 0`) &#x2014; except the "id" here is a **path string**, not a FK to another table (documents are not rows; they are discovered live from the filesystem). Composite PK becomes `(agent_id, path)` / `(skill_id, path)`.
- `repos.context_folders` &#x2014; new nullable `jsonb` (`text[]` is also viable; `jsonb` chosen to match the project's existing convention of `evidence_files: jsonb('evidence_files').$type<string[]>()` on `skills`) column, added via a new migration, never altering the existing `repos` table's other columns.
- `TEXT` for all path columns (never `VARCHAR(n)`), matching `postgresql-table-design` guidance and the existing `symbols.name`/`skills.name` convention.

**`react-best-practices` / `frontend-architecture` / `next-best-practices`:**
- `ContextTab` and the Project Context page are client components (`"use client"`) using TanStack Query hooks only &#x2014; no `useEffect` for data fetching.
- Reorder drag-and-drop reuses the exact pattern already in `SkillsTab.tsx` (`draggable`, `onDragStart`/`onDragOver`/`onDragEnd`, `moveUp`/`moveDown`-style array splice) &#x2014; no new drag library.
- The live serialization preview (AC-9) is a pure computed value from already-fetched query data (`useMemo` only if measured expensive &#x2014; for a handful of documents, plain inline computation is fine, no premature `useMemo`).
- Page route follows the existing `_components/<Name>/` colocation convention.
- Dead-code removal respects the promotion/ownership rule in reverse: code with zero live consumers is removed rather than kept "just in case" &#x2014; carrying unreachable exports is its own architecture smell.

## 4. Project Constraints

- **Server:** new module = Fastify plugin in `src/modules/context-docs/`; registered statically in `modules/index.ts` &#x2014; no auto-discovery. Adapters via `app.container` only. Route schemas via Zod + `fastify-type-provider-zod`. Expected failures throw `AppError` subclasses.
- **DB:** two new tables (`agent_context_docs`, `skill_context_docs`) + one new column (`repos.context_folders`) via **one** new numbered migration (`0013_context_documents.sql`) &#x2014; never alter existing columns. Every domain table gets a non-nullable `workspace_id`... **exception documented**: the two link tables intentionally have NO direct `workspace_id` column (mirroring `agent_skills`, which also has none) because tenancy is enforced transitively through the `agent_id`/`skill_id` FK's owning row, which IS workspace-scoped &#x2014; every repository query joins through the owner table and filters on its `workspace_id`. This exception is explicitly called out per `server/src/db/AGENTS.md` review expectations.
- **`reviewer-core`:** zero I/O &#x2014; confirmed no change needed to `prompt.ts` itself; the `specs` slot and `wrapUntrusted` already exist. `INJECTION_GUARD` must not be touched. Grounding (`groundFindings()`) is unaffected &#x2014; context documents feed the prompt, not the finding-citation gate.
- **Shared types:** `ContextDocument`, `RunTraceContextDoc`, and the `RunTrace.context_documents` field are added to `server/src/vendor/shared/contracts/` AND mirrored byte-for-byte into `client/src/vendor/shared/contracts/` in the SAME step (per `client/insights.md` 2026-06-30 &#x2014; these silently diverge otherwise). In the SAME lockstep discipline, the dead `SpecFile`/`IndexStatus` deletion in Step 1 also touches both vendored copies together.
- **Security &#x2014; path confinement (AC-13):** a new pure helper `resolveConfinedPath(cloneRoot, contextFolders, storedPath)` in `context-docs/helpers.ts` MUST reject: (a) any resolved absolute path that does not start with `cloneRoot + path.sep` (blocks `../../secret` traversal and symlink-adjacent tricks via `path.resolve` normalization), and (b) any path whose first segment is not one of the configured `context_folders`. This is a new mechanical check &#x2014; no existing helper in the repo does this; do not reuse `path.join` alone (per the `security` skill: `path.join()` with user input allows traversal &#x2014; use `path.resolve()` + prefix check, never `path.basename()` alone since we need to preserve subdirectory structure).
- **Security &#x2014; untrusted content (AC-11):** every injected document text goes through the EXISTING `wrapUntrusted('spec-N', text)` inside `assemblePrompt()` &#x2014; this plan does not re-implement wrapping; it only produces the `specs: string[]` array reviewer-core already accepts. No keyword filtering added (the project's `INJECTION_GUARD` is the only defense layer &#x2014; do not add a second one).
- **Security &#x2014; attacker-controlled input trace:** the document path is user-supplied at attach time (via the editor UI, same trust level as any other authenticated admin action in this single-tenant-per-workspace app) but is validated server-side at BOTH attach time (must resolve under a configured folder at the moment of attach &#x2014; reject unknown paths early with a clear 422) AND run time (AC-12/AC-13 &#x2014; re-validated fresh in case the repo changed between attach and run). Never trust the stored path blindly at read time.
- **Attachment scoping model (workspace-level path references):** attachments are stored on agents/skills as **workspace-level, repo-agnostic relative-path references** &#x2014; NOT repo-specific bindings (the link tables hold `(owner_id, path, order)`, no `repo_id`). The editor picker browses documents from an EXPLICIT, deterministic, user-visible selected repository (shell context / route state), but only the relative path is persisted. At review time the path is resolved against the repository of the PR being reviewed; if the file does not exist there, the attachment is skipped and recorded in Prompt Assembly as skipped/missing context (AC-12). So an attachment "hits" only in repositories that contain that path &#x2014; the intended, spec-aligned model (paths in metadata, never copied text). The picker MUST surface which repo is being browsed so the user understands the source.
- **Caching / performance (spec �7 &#x2264; 500 ms p95):** the discovery result (the `ContextDocument[]` list incl. per-document token counts) is cached server-side so the clone walk + re-tokenization of every `.md` does NOT run on every page load / Context-tab open. Cache key = `repoId` + the repo's current clone HEAD commit (from the git client / repo-intel index state) + a hash of the effective `context_folders`. Invalidation is implicit on resync (HEAD sha changes) and explicit on `setContextFolders` (folder change alters discovery scope). Keep it lightweight &#x2014; an in-process cache in `ContextDocsService` (or a tiny cache helper) suffices for the single-instance dev deployment; no new persistence table. `used_by_agents` is NOT cached with the file list (it changes on attach/detach independently of the clone) &#x2014; compute it per request via `usedByCounts` and merge onto the cached list.
- **Zero LLM calls (AC-3):** discovery, token counting, and injection preparation must not call any `container.llm(...)`. This is enforced structurally &#x2014; `context-docs/service.ts` never touches `container.llm`.
- **Determinism/reuse:** token counting reuses `container.tokenizer.count()` (existing `TiktokenTokenizer`) &#x2014; no new tokenizer, no LLM-based estimate.
- **Naming vs. the retired scaffold:** the new API surface uses `/repos/:id/context-docs` (not `/repos/:id/context` &#x2014; that path is reserved for the PAGE route, not an API route: no server route ever existed at `/repos/:id/context`, only a client stub referenced it, and that stub is deleted in Step 1). The new shared contract is named `ContextDocument` (not `SpecFile`, which is deleted). The new client query key is `["context-docs", repoId]` (not `["context", repoId]`, which is deleted along with `useContextFiles`). The page route `client/src/app/repos/[repoId]/context/page.tsx`, the `"context"` sidebar nav key, and the `context.json` i18n namespace file are KEPT and get new, real content &#x2014; this is intentional reuse of a route/nav/i18n identity, not a data-contract reuse.
- **i18n:** all new UI strings via next-intl. The Project Context page's strings go into the EXISTING `context.json` file (repurposed &#x2014; old keys replaced, not appended to), since that is the namespace the route/nav key already imply. Agent/skill editor strings go into the existing `agents.json`/`skills.json` namespaces as new keys, matching how the existing `skills.*` sub-keys live under the `agents` namespace.
- **Verification gate for the Step 1 cleanup specifically:** `pnpm typecheck` (both `server` and `client`), `pnpm build` (client), and existing unit tests must all pass after the deletions, AND a grep for each deleted symbol name (`SpecFile`, `IndexStatus` &#x2014; Zod one only, `useContextFiles`, `useReindexContext`) across `client/src` and `server/src` must return zero matches outside historical comments that are also being fixed in the same step. This gate is non-negotiable before Step 1 is considered done.

