## v2 &#x2014; Design-mock parity

**Requirements:** AC-22&#x2026;AC-36 (spec revised 2026-07-03; AC-34 added during plan review to close a gap in AC-33's "deleted" trigger; AC-35 added during plan review for the skill-editor Context tab; AC-36 added during plan review to guarantee the Context page works for ANY repo, including one with no readable clone &#x2014; see Step 15, Step 12).
**Builds on:** v1 Steps 1&#x2013;10 above (implemented, verified, uncommitted in the working tree). Do not re-open v1 steps; v2 steps only ADD to or, where explicitly stated, REWRITE a v1-owned file (the rewrite is called out per-step so ownership never overlaps two steps).
**Execution mode:** single-agent, continuing strictly after Step 10.

### v2 Context

v1 shipped a read-only Project Context page (single-column table + modal preview) and read-only run-time injection straight from the clone. It also shipped the agent editor's Context tab and a skill editor "Project context to use" section &#x2014; both as a two-section (linked list + separate available-documents list) attach/detach picker embedded directly inside the skill's `ConfigTab`. v2 achieves full design-mock parity across THREE surfaces:

1. **The Project Context page** &#x2014; rewritten into a two-panel master-detail layout with inline view/edit, upload, delete, and a coverage ring &#x2014; all backed by a new `doc_overrides` database table so the clone (hard-reset by `sync()` on every poll) never has to be written to.
2. **The attach/detach picker** (`ContextDocsList`, shared by both editors) &#x2014; redesigned from the v1 two-section layout into the mock's single unified checkbox list.
3. **The skill editor** &#x2014; gains its own dedicated "Context" tab (matching the agent editor and the mock's tab row), instead of the picker being embedded inside Config.

Every read path that currently reads "the document" &#x2014; discovery/listing, preview, and run-time injection &#x2014; must now resolve "effective content" as **overlay body if a `doc_overrides` row exists for that `(repo_id, path)`, otherwise the clone file** (AC-25). A document with an overlay but no clone file is "overlay-only" (AC-27) and is discovered purely from `doc_overrides`. A coverage percentage (distinct-agents-using � total-workspace-agents � 100) is added alongside the existing "used by N agents" count. Deletion of an overlay is supported (AC-34) with two branches: reverting to clone content (if a clone file exists) or removing the document entirely (if overlay-only).

### v2 Architecture Fit

- **`doc_overrides` table** (new migration `0014`) &#x2014; `(repo_id, path)` unique, `body text not null`, `version integer not null default 1`. No direct `workspace_id` column &#x2014; same documented exception as `agent_context_docs`/`skill_context_docs`: every query joins through `repos.workspace_id`.
- **`context-docs/repository.ts`** gains an overlay sub-repository's worth of methods (kept in the SAME repository class &#x2014; one more table owned by the same module, not a new module): `getOverlay(repoId, path)`, `listOverlays(repoId)`, `upsertOverlay(repoId, path, body)`, `deleteOverlay(repoId, path)` &#x2014; all workspace-scoped via a join to `repos`.
- **`context-docs/service.ts`** gains the overlay-preferring read path: `listDocuments` now merges the clone-discovered inventory with `listOverlays` (union of paths, overlay wins on conflict, `source` computed at merge time &#x2014; never stored), `previewDocument`/a new `getDocumentContent` prefers the overlay body, and new methods `saveDocument` (upsert) and `deleteDocument` (conditional revert-vs-remove per AC-34) are added. A new `coverage(workspaceId)` computation reuses `usedByCounts` and divides by a new `countWorkspaceAgents(workspaceId)` repository method.
- **`context-docs/routes.ts`** gains `PUT /repos/:id/context-docs` (create/upload &#x2014; body `{ path, body }`) and `DELETE /repos/:id/context-docs` (body `{ path }` &#x2014; AC-34); the v1 `GET /repos/:id/context-docs/preview` route is RENAMED to `GET /repos/:id/context-docs/content` (see Step 12).
- **`run-executor.ts`'s `buildContextDocs`** gains one overlay lookup per resolved path, tried BEFORE the existing `resolveConfinedPath` + `container.git.readFile` branch &#x2014; overlay content is used as-is when present (still subject to the same confinement check on the PATH, since a stored attachment path must still resolve under a configured folder; only the CONTENT source changes, not the path-safety gate).
- **Project Context page client** &#x2014; `ContextDocsView.tsx` and `styles.ts` are REWRITTEN (not extended) into a two-panel layout: `DocList` (left, replaces the table body) + `DocDetail` (right, new &#x2014; Preview/Edit toggle, `Markdown` render or `Textarea` edit, Save/Delete/Upload controls, `CircularScore` coverage ring). `PreviewModal` is retired (its read-only rendering logic moves into a new `DocPreviewPane`, consumed by `DocDetail`'s Preview mode AND the redesigned `ContextDocsList` picker). `FoldersConfig` is reused unchanged.
- **Picker client** &#x2014; `ContextDocsList.tsx` (shared by the agent Context tab and the new skill Context tab) is REDESIGNED from its v1 two-section layout into a single unified list: each row = drag handle + checkbox (checked = attached) + path + category badge + Preview button; header shows an "X of Y attached" pill + the browsed-repo badge + an order-matters hint. Only CHECKED (attached) rows are draggable/reorderable.
- **Skill editor client** &#x2014; `SkillDetail.tsx` gains a `context` tab entry (between `config` and `preview`) and a new `SkillDetail/ContextTab.tsx` that renders the shared `ContextDocsList`; `ConfigTab.tsx` loses its embedded v1 section (moved, not duplicated).

### v2 Skills & Patterns Applied

**`backend-onion-architecture`:**
- The overlay CRUD stays inside the EXISTING `context-docs` module &#x2014; it is the same bounded concept (context documents), not a new domain. Adding it to a fresh module would split one concept across two modules for no reason; `ContextDocsRepository`/`ContextDocsService` simply grow.
- `service.ts` still never imports concrete adapters; overlay reads/writes go through `this.repo` (the existing `ContextDocsRepository`), same as v1.
- `routes.ts` still only validates + delegates; the revert-vs-remove branching logic for delete (AC-34) is BUSINESS LOGIC and belongs in `service.ts`, not the route handler.

**`typescript-expert`:**
- `source: z.enum(['clone', 'overlay', 'overlay-only'])` added to `ContextDocument` &#x2014; additive field, existing consumers that destructure specific fields are unaffected; consumers that spread the whole object get the new field for free.
- `coverage: z.number().int().min(0).max(100)` &#x2014; additive, non-nullable (spec says "rendered `0` when the workspace has no agents" &#x2014; never `null`).
- The new `DocOverride`/edit-request/upload-request contracts follow the same "Zod schema + `z.infer` type together" pattern as v1's Step 3.

**`zod`:**
- `SaveContextDocBody = z.object({ path: z.string().min(1), body: z.string() })` &#x2014; `body` allowed to be an empty string (an empty document is valid per v1's existing "empty document &#x2192; 0 tokens" edge case, extended to overlays); `path` must be non-empty but is NOT re-validated for folder-confinement at the schema layer (that is a business rule checked in `service.ts` against the repo's configured folders, consistent with v1's existing attach-time-validation pattern already documented in v1 �4 "Security &#x2014; attacker-controlled input trace").
- `DeleteContextDocBody = z.object({ path: z.string().min(1) })`.

**`drizzle-orm-patterns` / `postgresql-table-design`:**
- `doc_overrides`: `repoId uuid not null references repos(id) on delete cascade`, `path text not null`, `body text not null`, `version integer not null default 1`, unique constraint on `(repo_id, path)` (mirrors the composite-PK pattern used for the v1 link tables, but here a plain `unique()` index is used rather than a composite PK since `id` &#x2014; a surrogate uuid PK &#x2014; is still useful for a single-row `RETURNING` on upsert; decision: use a surrogate `id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid()` PLUS a `unique(repo_id, path)` constraint, since upsert-by-natural-key with Drizzle's `.onConflictDoUpdate` needs a named unique constraint target anyway, and a surrogate id keeps `RETURNING id` simple for the version-bump read-back).
- Index on `repo_id` (`doc_overrides_repo_idx`) for the `listOverlays(repoId)` per-repo query, per `postgresql-table-design` FK-not-auto-indexed guidance.
- `TEXT` for `path` and `body` (never `VARCHAR(n)` &#x2014; `body` can be arbitrarily long markdown).
- Upsert via Drizzle's `.insert(...).onConflictDoUpdate({ target: [doc_overrides.repoId, doc_overrides.path], set: { body: ..., version: sql\`${doc_overrides.version} + 1\` } })` &#x2014; the mechanical "last write wins, bumped version" behavior the spec's edge-case table requires (�6 "Two saves race on the same document").

**`react-best-practices` / `frontend-architecture` / `next-best-practices`:**
- `DocDetail`'s Preview/Edit toggle is local `useState` &#x2014; no server round-trip to switch modes; Edit mode's initial textarea value comes from the already-fetched effective-content query (overlay-if-present-else-clone), never a separate "get me the raw clone file" call.
- Save is a `useMutation` that invalidates `["context-docs", repoId]` (list &#x2014; token count/source may have changed) AND the content-detail query key for that specific path &#x2014; satisfies AC-33's auto-refresh requirement via React Query's normal invalidate-on-mutate flow (no polling, no manual refetch button beyond the explicit "refresh" toolbar affordance in AC-32, which triggers the same invalidate).
- `CircularScore` (existing vendored component, confirmed present at `client/src/vendor/ui/primitives/CircularScore.tsx`) is reused as-is for the coverage ring &#x2014; no new charting component needed.
- `Markdown` (existing vendored component at `client/src/vendor/ui/primitives/Markdown.tsx`) is reused as-is for Preview-mode rendering &#x2014; no new markdown renderer.
- `Textarea` (existing vendored component at `client/src/vendor/ui/kit/Textarea.tsx`) is reused as-is for Edit mode &#x2014; confirm its props support a controlled `value`/`onChange` before wiring (verify by reading the file in Step 14; do not assume).
- `Checkbox` (existing vendored component, confirmed present at `client/src/vendor/ui/kit/Checkbox.tsx`, controlled `checked`/`onChange` props) is reused as-is for the redesigned `ContextDocsList` row &#x2014; no new checkbox component.
- `PreviewModal`'s retirement follows the promotion rule in reverse: a component whose only consumer's UX is being replaced is deleted, not kept "just in case" &#x2014; its consumers (the v1 `ContextDocsView` row action, replaced by the rewrite, and `ContextDocsList`'s preview control) are explicitly re-pointed at a small extracted `DocPreviewPane` (the read-only rendering half of the new `DocDetail`, factored out so the picker keeps a lightweight read-only preview without dragging in Edit-mode/Save/Delete/Upload UI it doesn't need).
- **Tab-set regression class (from the agent editor's own fixed history):** `client/src/app/agents/[id]/page.tsx` derives `VALID_TABS = TABS.map(t => t.key)` from the editor's own tab-definition array specifically because a prior version hardcoded a separate valid-tabs list that drifted from `TABS` (adding a tab to `TABS` without adding it to the gate silently reverted `?tab=context` to `config`). The skill editor's `SkillDetail.tsx` does NOT currently have an external `?tab=` URL-synced gate at all (v1: tab state is local `useState("config")`, no query-string persistence) &#x2014; so this specific regression class does not apply to it verbatim. What DOES carry over: `SkillDetail.tsx`'s `TABS` array (the rendered tab list) and its render switch (`{tab === "..." && <...Tab .../>}`) are two separate lists that must be kept in sync BY HAND (no derivation possible, since there's no separate gate array to derive from) &#x2014; Step 15 must add the `context` entry to BOTH in the same edit and a test must assert the tab is clickable and renders its content, closing the same class of drift the agent page's fix closed for its own two lists (`TABS` vs. render switch).
- **No-clone repo is a first-class case, not an error state:** `DocList`/`DocDetail` render identically whether the repo has a clone or not — a no-clone repo simply has zero `source: 'clone'`/`'overlay'` documents and only ever shows `source: 'overlay-only'` ones (plus whatever the user uploads going forward). No special "this repo has no clone" banner/empty-state branch is introduced in the client; the existing empty-state (zero documents) and populated-list rendering already cover it once the server-side fix (Step 12) stops discovery from silently returning nothing.

### v2 Project Constraints

- **DB &#x2014; exactly one new migration:** `server/src/db/migrations/0014_doc_overrides.sql`, additive only (`CREATE TABLE doc_overrides`), never touching `0013`'s tables or any other existing table/column. Per the coordinator's grounding note, `db:generate` is confirmed clean at the start of v2 (the drizzle snapshot chain was repaired in v1 Step 2) &#x2014; a straightforward `pnpm db:generate` run is expected to produce a clean `0014` with no manual snapshot surgery.
- **Clone stays strictly read-only (non-negotiable, restated from spec �7 and v1's Non-goals):** no v2 step may introduce a `container.git.writeFile`/commit/push call anywhere. Grep confirmation of this is part of every v2 step's Verify checklist that touches `service.ts` or `run-executor.ts`.
- **Overlay content is untrusted (AC-30):** the overlay-branch in `run-executor.ts`'s `buildContextDocs` feeds the SAME `specs: string[]` array as the clone-branch &#x2014; both go through `assemblePrompt()`'s existing `wrapUntrusted('spec-N', &#x2026;)` + `INJECTION_GUARD` unchanged. No new sanitization, no keyword filtering, no second guard layer (mirrors v1 �4's existing "no keyword filtering added" rule).
- **Read-path precedence is a single rule enforced in exactly one place per surface, never duplicated:** discovery (`listDocuments`), preview/content-fetch (`getDocumentContent`), and run-time injection (`buildContextDocs`) each independently call `this.repo.getOverlay(repoId, path)` (or the batched `listOverlays` for the list case) and prefer it &#x2014; but the "prefer overlay" DECISION LOGIC (if overlay exists, use its body and mark source accordingly) must be implemented as one small shared helper in `context-docs/helpers.ts` (e.g. `resolveEffectiveContent(cloneContent: string | undefined, overlayBody: string | undefined): { content: string; source: ContextDocument['source'] } | undefined`) &#x2014; NOT reimplemented three times with subtly different edge-case handling. This is a new mechanical helper, added in Step 11, consumed by Step 12 (service) and Step 13 (run-executor).
